:Ravioli|Ravioli]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Italy|Italian cuisine]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] finely-[[Cookbook:Dice|diced]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*¼ cup finely-diced [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]]\n*9 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] [[Cookbook:Crab|crab]] meat, fresh or canned (see notes)\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Dijon Mustard|Dijon mustard]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Heavy Cream|heavy cream]]\n*1 large [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], beaten\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n*2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*¼ cup [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|bread crumbs]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]] (if using fresh crabmeat)\n*¼ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n==Procedure==\n# [[Cookbook:Sautéing|Sauté]] the onion and garlic in the butter over low heat until soft, about 15 minutes.\n# Combine crab meat, mustard, cream, egg, lemon juice, parsley, bread crumbs and seasonings in a bowl.\n#Add the onion and celery and mix until well blended but not homogeneous.\n#Cover and refrigerate until the pasta dough is ready.\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* If using canned crab meat, drain in a sieve and taste. If excessively salty, rinse under running water until palatable.\n\n\n[[Category:Italian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes for filling]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using crab]]\n[[Category:Recipes using parsley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using salt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using Dijon mustard]]\n[[Category:Recipes using onion]]\n[[Category:Recipes using heavy cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Pescatarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Crab Meat Ravioli Filling","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"sour